{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/init(ksf:memoryKib:iterations:parallelism:logN:r:p:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/iterations","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/ksf","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/logN","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/p","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/parallelism","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/r"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/argon2id","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/scrypt"],"title":"Type Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KsfParams"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The cost properties are optional on purpose: they arrive flat, and a field that does not apply"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the named function is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent, not zero"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". Reading a missing "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/KsfParams\/memoryKib"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"type":"text","text":" would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stretch at the wrong cost and fail against a record that is perfectly good (§23.4 rule 5)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These are never cached across exchanges and never defaulted locally. A credential enrolled"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under one cost keeps working after a tenant raises its policy, so a client that guessed would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derive a different randomized password and report “invalid password” for one that is entirely"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"correct (§23.4 rule 2)."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"This is where Swift stopped needing a `pbkdf2_sha256` tenant","level":2,"anchor":"This-is-where-Swift-stopped-needing-a-pbkdf2sha256-tenant"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SRP client this replaces refused an "},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tenant outright: Swift has no Argon2 that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ships on every supported platform, and substituting PBKDF2 would have derived a different "},{"code":"x","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and surfaced as “invalid password”. AXIAM’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"default"}]},{"type":"text","text":" KDF was, for Swift, unreachable. The key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stretching now happens inside "},{"code":"libaxiam_opaque_ffi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"code":"argon2id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is no longer a Swift-shaped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hole — and "},{"code":"pbkdf2_sha256","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an OPAQUE key-stretching function at all."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:8Axia